cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  The Angular Observer: Scale-Invariant Coarse-Graining as a
  Universal Observer Basis for Emergent Geometry
abstract: >-
  Writing the graph normalized-Laplacian eigen-embedding in polar form, the
  angular coordinates of the low-eigenvalue subspace carry a graph's geodesic
  geometry while the radial coordinate is asymptotically geometry-free
  (von Luxburg degeneracy). Keeping only the angle — the Ng-Jordan-Weiss /
  PolarQuant move — is a measurable, universal model of a bounded observer's
  coarse-graining, holding across Wolfram-model rewriting, lattices, and
  embedding trajectories, and obeying a linear observer-fidelity-vs-dimension law.
